    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15607" root="رشم" body-key="r">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَشَمَ</span></b> , (S, K,) aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَشُمَ</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَشْمٌ</span>, (S,) <i>He
stamped,</i> or <i>sealed,</i> wheat. (S, K. [See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَوْشَمٌ</span>.])
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <i>He wrote;</i> (K, TA;) <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَلَيْهِ</span> [<i>upon it</i>],
and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِلَيْهِ</span> [<i>to him</i>]: accord. to the copies of the K,
like ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رشَم</span></b> ; but this is a mistake for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَسَمَ</span>, with the
unpointed <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">س</span> [and without teshdeed]. (TA.)

